  <section>
    <h2 id="quick-answer">Quick Answer</h2>
    <p><strong>bauma CHINA 2026 takes place in Shanghai from November 23–27, 2026, across two exhibition venues.</strong> If you're attending from outside China, the most important thing to know is that the venues have different exhibition dates.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Shanghai World Expo Exhibition &amp; Convention Center (SWEECC):</strong> November 23–26</li>
      <li><strong>Shanghai New International Expo Centre (SNIEC):</strong> November 24–27</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can visit both venues using the same visitor ticket, and the organizer will provide free shuttle buses between them.</p>
    <p>Admission is free if you register online in advance. Visitors who register on arrival pay RMB 80 (approximately USD 12).</p>
    <p>Before booking your trip, check which venue your preferred exhibitors will be at and whether you need a Chinese visa. Some international travelers may qualify for China's 240-hour visa-free transit policy.</p>
    <p class="cta"><strong><a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">Check your 240-hour transit eligibility →</a></strong></p>
  </section>

